GT_UNIT({"id":"if","title":"If-clauses","ruleTitle":"If-clauses","date":"2026-10-06","sets":{"b":[{"n":"Type 1: possible","p":["b1"]},{"n":"Type 2: imagined","p":["b2"]}],"k":[{"n":"Type 3: too late","p":["k1"]},{"n":"unless and when","p":["k2"]}],"p":[{"n":"I wish and should have","p":["p1"]},{"n":"Mixed types","p":["p2"]}]},"tags":{"T1":"Typ 1: if + simple present, will","T2":"Typ 2: if + simple past, would","T3":"Typ 3: if + had + dritte Form, would have","UN":"unless (= if … not)","WH":"when, as soon as, until: kein will","WI":"I wish (jetzt oder Vergangenheit)","SH":"should have + dritte Form","MX":"Gemischte Typen"},"coach":"Before you choose the forms, ask yourself how real it is. If it is possible, you need type 1. If you only imagine it, you need type 2. If it is too late, you need type 3.","quips":{"T1":["Will appears only once in a type 1 sentence, and it is never in the if-clause.","The if-clause takes the simple present, even when it is about tomorrow."],"T2":["This is only imagined, so the if-clause steps back to the simple past.","In a type 2 sentence would does not come after if. It waits in the other part."],"T3":["It is too late to change it, so the if-clause needs had and the third form.","If nobody had thrown me across the room, I would not have landed on the bookshelf. That was type 3."],"UN":["Unless already means \"if not\", so it does not need a second not."],"WH":["After when, as soon as and until you use the simple present, and will waits in the other part."],"WI":["A wish about now takes the simple past, and a wish about the past takes had and the third form."],"SH":["Should have and the third form means it was the right thing to do, and it did not happen."],"MX":["Look at each half on its own and ask whether it is about now or about the past."]},"tasks":{"b1":"Use type 1: simple present and will.","b2":"Use type 2: simple past and would.","bc":"Type 1 or type 2?","k1":"Use type 3: had + third form and would have.","k2":"Simple present or will?","kc":"Type 1, 2 or 3?","p1":"Now or past?","p2":"Each part: now or past?","pc":"Now or past?"},"card":{"top":["Possible, imagined or too late?","Possible → type 1. Imagined → type 2. Too late → type 3."],"lines":[{"s":"b1","r":"Type 1 (possible): if + simple present, will + base form","e":"[If] it {rains}, we <<will>> {stay} at home. // We <<will>> {stay} at home [if] it {rains}.","n":"No will after if: [If] it ~will rain~ {rains} // If-clause first → comma. If-clause second → no comma."},{"s":"b2","r":"Type 2 (imagined): if + simple past, would + base form","e":"[If] I {had} a car, I <<would>> {drive} you home. ^I have no car^","n":"No would after if: [If] I ~would have~ {had} a car // For advice: [If] I {were} you, I <<would>> …"},{"s":"k1","r":"Type 3 (too late): had + third form, would have + third form","e":"[If] I <<had>> {seen} your message, I <<would have>> {called} you. ^I did not see it^","n":"No would have after if: [If] I ~would have seen~ <<had>> {seen}"},{"s":"k2","r":"unless = if … not","e":"We <<will>> {miss} the bus [unless] we {leave} now. ^= if we do not leave now^"},{"s":"k2","r":"After when, as soon as, until → simple present, no will","e":"I <<will>> {text} you [when] I {arrive}.","n":"German „wenn“: sure to happen → [when] · only perhaps → [if]"},{"s":"p1","r":"I wish + simple past (now) or had + third form (past)","e":"I [wish] I {had} more time. ^now^ // I [wish] I <<had>> {studied} more. ^past^","n":"Also: [If only] I {had} more time!"},{"s":"p1","r":"should have + third form → it was a mistake not to do it","e":"You <<should have>> {told} me. ^you did not^","n":"Negative: I <<should not have>> {said} that. ^I said it^"},{"s":"p2","r":"Mixed: each part takes the form for its own time","e":"[If] I <<had>> {gone} to bed earlier, I <<would not>> {be} so tired [now]. ^past → now^ // [If] I {were} braver, I <<would have>> {asked} her [yesterday]. ^always → past^"}],"key":"<<blue>> helper verb · {red} verb form · [yellow] signal word"},"lessons":{"b1":{"t":"Type 1: possible","s":[{"b":"[If] it {rains}, we <<will>> {stay} at home.","t":"An if-sentence has two parts: a condition and a result. When the condition comes true, the result follows."},{"b":"[If] it {rains}, we <<will>> {stay} at home. ^possible^","t":"This one is type 1. Rain is really possible, so the speaker is talking about something that can happen."},{"b":"[if] + {simple present} // <<will>> + {base form}","t":"The if-clause takes the simple present, and the other part takes will and the base form."},{"b":"[If] it ~will rain~ {rains}, we <<will>> {stay} at home.","t":"Here is the trap. The rain is in the future too, but there is no will after if. Will appears only once, in the result.","m":"dry"},{"b":"[If] it {rains}, we <<will>> {stay} at home. // We <<will>> {stay} at home [if] it {rains}.","t":"You can turn the sentence around, and the meaning stays the same. Look at the comma: when the if-clause comes first, a comma follows it. When it comes second, there is none."}],"k":[[{"b":"If you ___ now, you will catch the bus.","t":"Which form fits?","o":["leave","will leave","leaving"],"c":0,"r":"Yes. The if-clause takes the simple present.","w":"No. There is no will in the if-clause. It takes the simple present: If you leave now, …"},{"b":"If she ___ this photo, she will be furious.","t":"Which form fits?","o":["will see","see","sees"],"c":2,"r":"Right. Simple present, and she takes -s.","w":"No. The if-clause takes the simple present, and she takes -s: If she sees this photo, …"}],[{"b":"[If] I {find} your keys, I <<will>> {call} you.","t":"Why \"find\" and not \"will find\"?","o":["Because there is no will in the if-clause.","Because the keys are lost.","Because find is an irregular verb."],"c":0,"r":"Exactly. Will appears only in the result.","w":"No. There is no will in the if-clause, even when it is about the future."},{"b":"He <<will>> {help} you [if] you {ask} him.","t":"Why \"ask\" and not \"will ask\"?","o":["Because he is a helpful person.","Because ask is a short verb.","Because the if-clause takes the simple present, even when it is about the future."],"c":2,"r":"Exactly. The simple present after if, and will in the other part.","w":"No. The if-clause takes the simple present, even when it is about the future. Will goes in the other part."}]]},"b2":{"t":"Type 2: imagined","s":[{"b":"[If] I {have} time, I <<will>> {help} you. ^possible^","t":"You know type 1: something can really happen. Type 2 is for the things you only imagine."},{"b":"[If] I {had} a car, I <<would>> {drive} you home. ^I have no car^","t":"The speaker has no car. It is a daydream about now, and English shows that by taking one step back in time."},{"b":"[if] + {simple past} // <<would>> + {base form}","t":"The if-clause takes the simple past, and the other part takes would and the base form. The simple past does not mean yesterday here. It means \"not real\"."},{"b":"Wenn ich ein Auto hätte, würde ich … // [If] I ~would have~ {had} a car, I <<would>> {drive} you home.","t":"German is happy with \"würde\" in both parts. English allows would only once, in the result, and not after if.","m":"dry"},{"b":"[If] I {were} you, I <<would>> {call} her.","t":"One phrase is worth learning by heart: If I were you. It is the usual way to give advice, and it takes were, not was."},{"b":"[If] I {have} time, … ^possible: type 1^ // [If] I {had} time, … ^only imagined: type 2^","t":"So the choice between type 1 and type 2 is a choice about how real it is. Possible takes type 1, and imagined takes type 2."}],"k":[[{"b":"If I ___ rich, I would buy the whole street.","t":"Which form fits?","o":["would be","were","am"],"c":1,"r":"Yes. The if-clause steps back to the simple past.","w":"No. There is no would in the if-clause. It takes the simple past: If I were rich, …"},{"b":"If we had a garden, we ___ a dog.","t":"Which form fits?","o":["would get","got","will get"],"c":0,"r":"Right. Would and the base form go in the result.","w":"No. \"Had\" shows that it is only imagined, so the result takes would: we would get a dog."}],[{"b":"[If] she {knew} the answer, she <<would>> {tell} us.","t":"Why \"knew\" and not \"would know\"?","o":["Because there is no would in the if-clause.","Because she has forgotten the answer.","Because know is an irregular verb."],"c":0,"r":"Exactly. Would appears only in the result.","w":"No. There is no would in the if-clause. It takes the simple past: knew."},{"b":"[If] I {had} more money, I <<would>> {travel} more.","t":"What does this sentence tell you?","o":["The speaker travelled a lot last year.","The speaker does not have much money at the moment.","The speaker is saving for a trip."],"c":1,"r":"Exactly. Type 2 imagines something that is not real now.","w":"No. Type 2 is about now, and it imagines something that is not real: the speaker does not have much money."}]]},"k1":{"t":"Type 3: too late","s":[{"b":"[If] I {had} a car, I <<would>> {drive} you home. ^imagined, now^","t":"Type 2 imagines a different present. Type 3 goes one step further and imagines a different past."},{"b":"I did not see your message. I did not call you.","t":"Here is what really happened. It is over, and nobody can change it. But you can still imagine the opposite."},{"b":"[If] I <<had>> {seen} your message, I <<would have>> {called} you. ^I did not see it^","t":"That is type 3. The if-clause takes had and the third form, and the other part takes would have and the third form."},{"b":"[if] + <<had>> + {third form} // <<would have>> + {third form}","t":"You know both pieces. Had and the third form is the past perfect, and the third form is the one from the present perfect: seen, gone, called."},{"b":"[If] I ~would have seen~ <<had>> {seen} your message, …","t":"The trap is the same as before. Would does not follow if, so \"if I would have seen\" is wrong, however often you hear it.","m":"dry"},{"b":"possible → type 1 // imagined → type 2 // too late → type 3","t":"That gives you all three. Ask yourself whether it is possible, only imagined, or too late."}],"k":[[{"b":"If we ___ earlier, we would have got better seats.","t":"Which form fits?","o":["had arrived","would have arrived","arrived"],"c":0,"r":"Yes. Had and the third form after if.","w":"No. It is too late, so the if-clause takes had and the third form: If we had arrived earlier, …"},{"b":"If you had asked me, I ___ yes.","t":"Which form fits?","o":["said","would have said","would say"],"c":1,"r":"Right. Would have and the third form go in the result.","w":"No. \"Had asked\" shows that it is too late, so the result takes would have: I would have said yes."}],[{"b":"[If] he <<had>> {trained}, he <<would have>> {won}.","t":"What really happened?","o":["He did not train, and he did not win.","He trained, but he did not win.","He is going to train next time."],"c":0,"r":"Exactly. Type 3 describes the opposite of what happened.","w":"No. Type 3 describes the opposite of what happened: he did not train, and he did not win."},{"b":"[If] it <<had>> not {rained}, we <<would have>> {gone} out.","t":"What really happened?","o":["It did not rain, and we went out.","It rained, and we stayed in.","It may rain later."],"c":1,"r":"Exactly. Type 3 describes the opposite of what happened.","w":"No. Type 3 describes the opposite of what happened: it rained, and we stayed in."}]]},"k2":{"t":"unless and when","s":[{"b":"We <<will>> {miss} the bus [if] we do not {leave} now.","t":"Two more words can open a condition. The first one is unless."},{"b":"We <<will>> {miss} the bus [unless] we {leave} now. ^= if we do not leave now^","t":"Unless means \"if not\". The not is already inside the word, so you do not add another one."},{"b":"~unless we don't leave~ [unless] we {leave}","t":"That is the usual slip: two negatives where one is enough.","m":"dry"},{"b":"I <<will>> {text} you [when] I {arrive}.","t":"The second word is when. It follows the same rule as if: the simple present comes after it, and will appears only in the other part."},{"b":"[when] · [as soon as] · [until] // I <<will>> {wait} [until] you {come}.","t":"As soon as and until behave in the same way. None of them takes will."},{"b":"Wenn ich ankomme, … // [When] I {arrive}, … ^sure to happen^ // [If] I {arrive} in time, … ^only perhaps^","t":"German has one word for both: \"wenn\". English makes you choose. When is for things that are sure to happen, and if is for things that may or may not happen."}],"k":[[{"b":"I will call you as soon as I ___ anything.","t":"Which form fits?","o":["will hear","hear","heard"],"c":1,"r":"Yes. The simple present after as soon as.","w":"No. After as soon as there is no will. It takes the simple present: as soon as I hear anything."},{"b":"We will not start until everybody ___ here.","t":"Which form fits?","o":["is","will be","would be"],"c":0,"r":"Right. The simple present after until.","w":"No. After until there is no will. It takes the simple present: until everybody is here."}],[{"b":"You will not pass [unless] you {study}.","t":"What does this sentence mean?","o":["You will not pass if you do not study.","You will not pass if you study.","You will pass when you stop studying."],"c":0,"r":"Exactly. Unless means \"if not\".","w":"No. Unless means \"if not\": you will not pass if you do not study."},{"b":"I <<will>> {tell} her [when] she {comes} home.","t":"Why \"when\" and not \"if\"?","o":["Because she is angry.","Because the speaker is sure that she will come home.","Because when is more polite than if."],"c":1,"r":"Exactly. When is for things that are sure to happen.","w":"No. The speaker is sure that she will come home, and that takes when. If would mean that it is only possible."}]]},"p1":{"t":"Wishes and regrets","s":[{"b":"[If] I {had} more time, I <<would>> {help} you. ^imagined^","t":"You know how English talks about things that are not real: it takes one step back in time. \"I wish\" works in exactly the same way."},{"b":"I [wish] I {had} more time. ^now^","t":"This is a wish about now. The speaker has no time, and so the verb steps back to the simple past: I wish I had."},{"b":"I [wish] I <<had>> {studied} more. ^past^","t":"This is a wish about the past. It is too late, as in type 3, so the verb steps back once more: had and the third form."},{"b":"I [wish] I {had} more time. ^now^ // I [wish] I <<had>> {studied} more. ^past^","t":"Now takes the simple past, and the past takes had and the third form. \"I wish I would have\" is not English. \"If only\" works the same way: If only I had more time!"},{"b":"You <<should have>> {told} me. ^you did not^","t":"There is a second way to talk about a mistake in the past: should have and the third form. It means that this was the right thing to do, and that it did not happen."},{"b":"I <<should not have>> {said} that. ^I said it^","t":"With not it turns around. The thing happened, and it was a mistake."}],"k":[[{"b":"I wish I ___ a bigger room.","t":"Which form fits?","o":["would have","had","have"],"c":1,"r":"Yes. A wish about now takes the simple past.","w":"No. A wish about now takes the simple past, not would: I wish I had a bigger room."},{"b":"I wish I ___ that film. I had nightmares all night.","t":"Which form fits?","o":["didn’t watch","wouldn’t watch","hadn’t watched"],"c":2,"r":"Right. A wish about the past takes had and the third form.","w":"No. The film is over, so this is a wish about the past: I wish I hadn’t watched that film."}],[{"b":"We <<should have>> {booked} a table.","t":"What really happened?","o":["We did not book a table.","We booked a table.","We are going to book a table."],"c":0,"r":"Exactly. Should have means that it did not happen.","w":"No. Should have and the third form means that it was the right thing to do, and that it did not happen."},{"b":"She <<should not have>> {opened} the letter.","t":"What really happened?","o":["She did not open the letter.","She opened the letter, and it was a mistake.","She is going to open the letter."],"c":1,"r":"Exactly. Should not have means that it happened, and that it was a mistake.","w":"No. Should not have and the third form means that it happened, and that it was a mistake."}]]},"p2":{"t":"Two times in one sentence","s":[{"b":"[If] I <<had>> {gone} to bed earlier, I <<would have>> {felt} better [yesterday]. ^past → past^","t":"In type 3 both parts are about the past. But a mistake in the past can have a result that you still feel now."},{"b":"[If] I <<had>> {gone} to bed earlier, I <<would not>> {be} so tired [now]. ^past → now^","t":"Look at the two halves. Going to bed is in the past, so it takes had and the third form. Being tired is now, so it takes would and the base form."},{"b":"past: <<had>> + {third form} · <<would have>> + {third form} // now or always: {simple past} · <<would>> + {base form}","t":"Each part simply takes the form for its own time. You do not need a new rule, only the two you already have."},{"b":"[If] I {were} braver, I <<would have>> {asked} her [yesterday]. ^always → past^","t":"It works the other way round too. Not being brave is true all the time, so it takes the simple past. Yesterday is the past, so the result takes would have and the third form."},{"b":"[now] [today] [still] → <<would>> + {base form} // [yesterday] [last night] [this morning] → <<would have>> + {third form}","t":"Time words are your best clue. Check each half of the sentence on its own and ask whether it is about now or about the past."}],"k":[[{"b":"If I had worn a jacket, I ___ so cold now.","t":"Which form fits?","o":["wouldn’t have been","wouldn’t be","won’t be"],"c":1,"r":"Yes. The result is about now.","w":"No. \"Now\" shows that the result is about the present: I wouldn’t be so cold now."},{"b":"If I ___ you better, I would have asked you yesterday.","t":"Which form fits?","o":["knew","know","would know"],"c":0,"r":"Right. Knowing somebody is a general thing.","w":"No. There is no would after if, and knowing somebody is a general thing, so it takes the simple past: If I knew you better, …"}],[{"b":"[If] she <<had>> {taken} the job, she <<would>> {live} in Rome [now].","t":"Why \"would live\" and not \"would have lived\"?","o":["Because living in Rome is about now.","Because Rome is far away.","Because she took the job."],"c":0,"r":"Exactly. A result that is about now takes would and the base form.","w":"No. \"Now\" shows that the result is about the present, and that takes would and the base form."},{"b":"[If] he {were} taller, he <<would have>> {reached} the shelf [this morning].","t":"Why \"were\" and not \"had been\"?","o":["Because the shelf is too high.","Because his height is a general thing and not something from this morning.","Because he is still growing."],"c":1,"r":"Exactly. A general thing takes the simple past.","w":"No. His height is a general thing. It is true all the time, so the if-clause takes the simple past."}]]}},"items":[{"i":"e-01","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"If it rains tomorrow, we ___ (watch) the match at my place.","f":"","g":"","a":[["'ll watch","'re going to watch","are going to watch","will watch"]],"h":["will watch"]},{"i":"e-02","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"I will lend you my bike if you ___ (bring) it back before six.","f":"","g":"","a":[["bring"]],"h":["bring"]},{"i":"e-03","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"If I ___ (have) a million euros, I would buy the flat next door and turn it into a cinema.","f":"","g":"","a":[["had"]],"h":["had"]},{"i":"e-04","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"If my brother were a bit nicer, I ___ (share) my snacks with him.","f":"","g":"","a":[["'d share","would share"]],"h":["would share"]},{"i":"e-05","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"If I ___ (know) about the test, I would have studied. Probably.","f":"","g":"","a":[["'d known","had known"]],"h":["had known"]},{"i":"e-06","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"If you had told me earlier, I ___ (bake) a cake. Now you get toast.","f":"","g":"","a":[["'d have baked","would have baked","would've baked"]],"h":["would have baked"]},{"i":"e-07","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"I will call you as soon as I ___ (get) home. Keep your phone on.","f":"","g":"","a":[["get"]],"h":["get"]},{"i":"e-08","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"You won't pass unless you ___ (start) revising soon. Sorry, somebody had to say it.","f":"","g":"","a":[["start"]],"h":["start"]},{"i":"e-09","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"I wish I ___ (have) a dog. Our flat is too small, apparently.","f":"","g":"","a":[["had"]],"h":["had"]},{"i":"e-10","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"I wish I ___ (not / eat) that third burger last night. I still feel sick.","f":"","g":"","a":[["had not eaten","hadn't eaten"]],"h":["had not eaten"]},{"i":"e-11","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"You ___ (should / warn) me about your dog. He ate my sandwich in one bite.","f":"","g":"","a":[["should have warned","should've warned"]],"h":["should have warned"]},{"i":"e-12","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"If I had charged my phone last night, I ___ (not / be) lost in this forest now.","f":"","g":"","a":[["would not be","wouldn't be"]],"h":["would not be"]},{"i":"b1-01","s":"b1","t":"mc","x":"If you ___ me one more time, I ___ my phone off.","f":"Type 1: simple present in the if-clause, will in the other part.","g":"T1","c":"text … will turn","w":["will text … will turn","will text … turn"]},{"i":"b1-02","s":"b1","t":"mc","x":"We ___ the bus if you ___ looking for your other shoe.","f":"There is no \"will\" in the if-clause: if you don't stop.","g":"T1","c":"will miss … don't stop","w":["miss … won't stop","will miss … won't stop"]},{"i":"b1-03","s":"b1","t":"mc","x":"If it ___ at the weekend, the festival ___ a swimming pool.","f":"Type 1: if + simple present, will + base form.","g":"T1","c":"rains … will turn into","w":["will rain … turns into","will rain … will turn into"]},{"i":"b1-04","s":"b1","t":"mc","x":"What ___ you ___ if nobody comes to your party?","f":"The question is built with will + subject + base form: What will you do …?","g":"T1","c":"will … do","w":["do … will","will … doing"]},{"i":"b1-05","s":"b1","t":"mc","x":"You promise to help a friend. Which sentence is correct?","f":"There is no \"will\" in the if-clause: If I have time, I will help you.","g":"T1","c":"If I have time tonight, I will help you.","w":["If I will have time tonight, I help you.","If I will have time tonight, I will help you."]},{"i":"b1-06","s":"b1","t":"mc","x":"My mum ___ furious if she ___ this mess.","f":"\"My mum\" is she, so the if-clause has \"sees\". \"Will\" goes in the other part.","g":"T1","c":"will be … sees","w":["is … will see","will be … will see"]},{"i":"b1-07","s":"b1","t":"mc","x":"Which sentence is punctuated correctly?","f":"When the if-clause comes first, a comma follows it. When it comes second, there is no comma.","g":"T1","c":"If you press that button, everything will go dark.","w":["Everything will go dark, if you press that button.","If you press that button everything will go dark."]},{"i":"b1-08","s":"b1","t":"mc","x":"If the shop ___ the price again, I ___ those headphones.","f":"Type 1: if + simple present, will + base form.","g":"T1","c":"drops … will buy","w":["will drop … buy","will drop … will buy"]},{"i":"b1-09","s":"b1","t":"mc","x":"Should 16-year-olds vote? Supporters say: \"If they ___ a vote, politicians ___ to them.\" Critics say it will change nothing.","f":"Type 1: if + simple present, will + base form.","g":"T1","c":"get … will listen","w":["will get … listen","will get … will listen"]},{"i":"b1-10","s":"b1","t":"gap","x":"If you ___ (tell) anyone, I ___ (never / speak) to you again.","f":"Type 1: if + simple present, will + base form.","g":"T1","a":[["tell"],["'ll never speak","will never speak"]],"h":["tell","will never speak"]},{"i":"b1-11","s":"b1","t":"gap","x":"My dad ___ (go) crazy if I ___ (scratch) his car. So I am walking.","f":"\"Will\" goes in the main part. The if-clause takes the simple present.","g":"T1","a":[["'ll go","will go"],["scratch"]],"h":["will go","scratch"]},{"i":"b1-12","s":"b1","t":"gap","x":"If she ___ (not / reply) by tonight, I ___ (delete) my message and move to another country.","f":"The if-clause takes the simple present: does not reply. \"Will\" goes in the other part.","g":"T1","a":[["does not reply","doesn't reply"],["'ll delete","will delete"]],"h":["does not reply","will delete"]},{"i":"b1-13","s":"b1","t":"gap","x":"If the bus ___ (be) late again, we ___ (miss) the first ten minutes of the film.","f":"Type 1: if + simple present, will + base form.","g":"T1","a":[["is"],["'ll miss","will miss"]],"h":["is","will miss"]},{"i":"b1-14","s":"b1","t":"gap","x":"What ___ (you / say) if your parents ___ (find) out?","f":"The question has will + subject + base form. The if-clause takes the simple present.","g":"T1","a":[["will you say"],["find"]],"h":["will you say","find"]},{"i":"b1-15","s":"b1","t":"gap","x":"Scientists warn that if sea levels ___ (keep) rising, some low islands ___ (disappear) under water.","f":"Type 1: if + simple present, will + base form.","g":"T1","a":[["keep"],["'ll disappear","will disappear"]],"h":["keep","will disappear"]},{"i":"b1-16","s":"b1","t":"gap","x":"I ___ (not / come) to training if it ___ (snow) again. My boots have a hole.","f":"\"Will not\" goes in the main part. The if-clause takes the simple present: snows.","g":"T1","a":[["will not come","won't come"],["snows"]],"h":["will not come","snows"]},{"i":"b1-17","s":"b1","t":"fix","x":"If you *will give* me your password, I will fix it for you.","f":"There is no \"will\" in the if-clause: If you give me …","g":"T1","a":[["give"]],"h":["give"]},{"i":"b1-18","s":"b1","t":"fix","x":"If my sister *finds* her birthday present under my bed, the surprise will be over.","f":"The if-clause takes the simple present, so \"finds\" is correct.","g":"T1","a":[["OK"]],"h":["OK"]},{"i":"b2-01","s":"b2","t":"mc","x":"If I ___ a time machine, I ___ back and skip that haircut.","f":"Type 2: if + simple past, would + base form.","g":"T2","c":"had … would go","w":["would have … went","have … would go"]},{"i":"b2-02","s":"b2","t":"mc","x":"If I ___ you, I ___ that message. You will regret it.","f":"\"If I were you\" is the usual way to give advice. \"Would\" goes in the other part.","g":"T2","c":"were … wouldn't send","w":["would be … didn't send","am … wouldn't send"]},{"i":"b2-03","s":"b2","t":"mc","x":"What ___ you ___ if you found 500 euros on the bus?","f":"\"Found\" is simple past, so this is type 2: What would you do …?","g":"T2","c":"would … do","w":["did … do","will … do"]},{"i":"b2-04","s":"b2","t":"mc","x":"My life ___ easier if my little brother ___ how to knock.","f":"There is no \"would\" in the if-clause: if my little brother knew.","g":"T2","c":"would be … knew","w":["was … would know","would be … would know"]},{"i":"b2-05","s":"b2","t":"mc","x":"Which sentence tells you that the speaker has no dog?","f":"Type 2 is for things you only imagine. Type 1 is for things that can really happen.","g":"T2","c":"If I had a dog, I would call it Pixel.","w":["If I get a dog, I will call it Pixel."]},{"i":"b2-06","s":"b2","t":"mc","x":"If my cat ___ English, she ___ about the food every single day.","f":"Type 2: if + simple past, would + base form.","g":"T2","c":"spoke … would complain","w":["would speak … complained","speaks … would complain"]},{"i":"b2-07","s":"b2","t":"mc","x":"You dream about a different life. Which sentence is correct?","f":"There is no \"would\" in the if-clause: If we lived by the sea …","g":"T2","c":"If we lived by the sea, I would surf every day.","w":["If we would live by the sea, I would surf every day.","If we would live by the sea, I surfed every day."]},{"i":"b2-08","s":"b2","t":"mc","x":"I ___ you if I ___ the answer, but I have no idea either.","f":"\"Would\" goes in the main part. The if-clause takes the simple past: knew.","g":"T2","c":"would tell … knew","w":["told … would know","would tell … would know"]},{"i":"b2-09","s":"b2","t":"mc","x":"If school ___ at ten, I ___ awake in the first lesson.","f":"Type 2: if + simple past, would + base form.","g":"T2","c":"started … would be","w":["would start … was","starts … would be"]},{"i":"b2-10","s":"b2","t":"gap","x":"If I ___ (have) wings, I ___ (fly) to school and still be late.","f":"Type 2: if + simple past, would + base form.","g":"T2","a":[["had"],["'d fly","would fly"]],"h":["had","would fly"]},{"i":"b2-11","s":"b2","t":"gap","x":"If my parents ___ (know) my screen time, they ___ (take) my phone away for ever.","f":"Type 2: if + simple past, would + base form.","g":"T2","a":[["knew"],["'d take","would take"]],"h":["knew","would take"]},{"i":"b2-12","s":"b2","t":"gap","x":"I ___ (not / tell) him if I ___ (be) you. He can't keep a secret.","f":"\"Would not\" goes in the main part. The if-clause is \"if I were you\".","g":"T2","a":[["would not tell","wouldn't tell"],["were"]],"h":["would not tell","were"]},{"i":"b2-13","s":"b2","t":"gap","x":"What ___ (you / do) if you ___ (win) a million euros tomorrow?","f":"The question has would + subject + base form. The if-clause takes the simple past: won.","g":"T2","a":[["would you do"],["won"]],"h":["would you do","won"]},{"i":"b2-14","s":"b2","t":"gap","x":"If I ___ (not / have) to get up at six, I ___ (be) a much friendlier person.","f":"The negative in the simple past is \"did not have\". \"Would\" goes in the other part.","g":"T2","a":[["did not have","didn't have"],["'d be","would be"]],"h":["did not have","would be"]},{"i":"b2-15","s":"b2","t":"gap","x":"If our team ___ (train) more often, we ___ (lose) a bit less.","f":"Type 2: if + simple past, would + base form.","g":"T2","a":[["trained"],["'d lose","would lose"]],"h":["trained","would lose"]},{"i":"b2-16","s":"b2","t":"gap","x":"If I had my brother's voice, I ___ (not / sing) in the shower. The neighbours have complained twice.","f":"\"Would not\" + base form goes in the main part.","g":"T2","a":[["would not sing","wouldn't sing"]],"h":["would not sing"]},{"i":"b2-17","s":"b2","t":"fix","x":"If I *would have* more time, I would learn the drums.","f":"There is no \"would\" in the if-clause: If I had more time …","g":"T2","a":[["had"]],"h":["had"]},{"i":"b2-18","s":"b2","t":"fix","x":"If we *lived* closer to school, I would get up at ten to eight.","f":"The if-clause takes the simple past, so \"lived\" is correct.","g":"T2","a":[["OK"]],"h":["OK"]},{"i":"bc-01","s":"bc","t":"mc","x":"If you ___ the plants this week, they ___.","f":"There is no \"will\" in the if-clause: if you don't water them.","g":"T1","c":"don't water … will die","w":["won't water … die","won't water … will die"]},{"i":"bc-02","s":"bc","t":"mc","x":"If I ___ the president, I ___ Mondays.","f":"This is only imagined, so it is type 2: if + simple past, would + base form.","g":"T2","c":"were … would ban","w":["would be … banned","were … will ban"]},{"i":"bc-03","s":"bc","t":"mc","x":"Which sentence tells you that the speaker really expects to have time?","f":"Type 1 is for things that can really happen. Type 2 is only imagined.","g":"T1","c":"If I have time, I will come to your match.","w":["If I had time, I would come to your match."]},{"i":"bc-04","s":"bc","t":"mc","x":"I ___ you a lift if my moped ___ a second seat. It doesn't, sorry.","f":"The moped has no second seat, so this is only imagined: type 2.","g":"T2","c":"would give … had","w":["will give … has","would give … would have"]},{"i":"bc-05","s":"bc","t":"mc","x":"You warn a friend. Which sentence is correct?","f":"There is no \"will\" in the if-clause, and no comma when the if-clause comes second.","g":"T1","c":"You will be tired tomorrow if you stay up all night.","w":["You will be tired tomorrow, if you will stay up all night.","You are tired tomorrow if you will stay up all night."]},{"i":"bc-06","s":"bc","t":"gap","x":"If you ___ (not / hurry), we will miss the beginning.","f":"\"Will\" in the main part shows type 1, so the if-clause takes the simple present.","g":"T1","a":[["do not hurry","don't hurry"]],"h":["do not hurry"]},{"i":"bc-07","s":"bc","t":"gap","x":"I ___ (lend) you the money if I had any. Look at my wallet.","f":"\"Had\" shows type 2, so the main part takes would + base form.","g":"T2","a":[["'d lend","would lend"]],"h":["would lend"]},{"i":"bc-08","s":"bc","t":"gap","x":"If my grandma ___ (see) my search history, she would faint.","f":"\"Would\" shows type 2, so the if-clause takes the simple past: saw.","g":"T2","a":[["saw"]],"h":["saw"]},{"i":"bc-09","s":"bc","t":"gap","x":"We ___ (not / get) a table if we arrive after eight. That place is always full.","f":"\"Arrive\" is simple present, so this is type 1: will not + base form.","g":"T1","a":[["will not get","won't get"]],"h":["will not get"]},{"i":"bc-10","s":"bc","t":"gap","x":"If it ___ (stop) raining, I will walk the dog. If it doesn't, the dog will have to walk himself.","f":"\"Will\" in the main part shows type 1, so the if-clause takes the simple present: stops.","g":"T1","a":[["stops"]],"h":["stops"]},{"i":"bc-11","s":"bc","t":"fix","x":"If I *would be* taller, I would play basketball.","f":"There is no \"would\" in the if-clause: If I were taller …","g":"T2","a":[["was","were"]],"h":["were"]},{"i":"bc-12","s":"bc","t":"gap","x":"If I were you, I ___ (say) sorry. If you wait too long, it ___ (get) awkward.","f":"\"If I were you\" is type 2: would say. \"If you wait\" is type 1: will get.","g":"T2","a":[["'d say","would say"],["'ll get","will get"]],"h":["would say","will get"]},{"i":"k1-01","s":"k1","t":"mc","x":"If I ___ my alarm, I ___ the bus.","f":"Type 3: if + had + third form, would have + third form.","g":"T3","c":"had heard … would have caught","w":["would have heard … had caught","would have heard … would have caught"]},{"i":"k1-02","s":"k1","t":"mc","x":"We ___ if our goalkeeper ___ awake.","f":"There is no \"would have\" in the if-clause: if he had stayed awake.","g":"T3","c":"would have won … had stayed","w":["had won … would have stayed","would have won … would have stayed"]},{"i":"k1-03","s":"k1","t":"mc","x":"Which sentence tells you that the speaker did not go to the party?","f":"Type 3 looks back at something that did not happen. It is too late to change it.","g":"T3","c":"If I had gone to the party, I would have met her.","w":["If I go to the party, I will meet her."]},{"i":"k1-04","s":"k1","t":"mc","x":"If you ___ me, I ___ you. Why didn't you say anything?","f":"Type 3: if + had + third form, would have + third form.","g":"T3","c":"had asked … would have helped","w":["would have asked … had helped","would have asked … would have helped"]},{"i":"k1-05","s":"k1","t":"mc","x":"I ___ that message if I ___ it was from your mum.","f":"\"Would have\" goes in the main part. The if-clause takes had + third form.","g":"T3","c":"wouldn't have opened … had known","w":["hadn't opened … would have known","wouldn't have opened … would have known"]},{"i":"k1-06","s":"k1","t":"mc","x":"You missed a concert last week. Which sentence is correct?","f":"There is no \"would have\" in the if-clause: If I had bought …","g":"T3","c":"If I had bought a ticket in time, I would have seen them live.","w":["If I would have bought a ticket in time, I would have seen them live.","If I had bought a ticket in time, I will have seen them live."]},{"i":"k1-07","s":"k1","t":"mc","x":"If Germany ___ the semi-final against Brazil in 2014, it ___ in the final.","f":"Type 3: if + had + third form, would have + third form.","g":"T3","c":"had lost … would not have played","w":["would have lost … had not played","would have lost … would not have played"]},{"i":"k1-08","s":"k1","t":"mc","x":"What ___ you ___ if your mum had seen that message?","f":"\"Had seen\" shows type 3, so the question is: What would you have done?","g":"T3","c":"would … have done","w":["had … done","would … did"]},{"i":"k1-09","s":"k1","t":"mc","x":"Which sentence tells you that it rained?","f":"\"If it hadn't rained\" looks back: it did rain. Type 3 always describes the opposite of what happened.","g":"T3","c":"If it hadn't rained, we would have had the party in the garden.","w":["If it doesn't rain, we will have the party in the garden."]},{"i":"k1-10","s":"k1","t":"gap","x":"If I ___ (know) you were coming, I ___ (tidy) my room. A little.","f":"Type 3: if + had + third form, would have + third form.","g":"T3","a":[["'d known","had known"],["'d have tidied","would have tidied","would've tidied"]],"h":["had known","would have tidied"]},{"i":"k1-11","s":"k1","t":"gap","x":"If you ___ (not / post) that photo, nobody ___ (find) out.","f":"Type 3: if + had + third form, would have + third form.","g":"T3","a":[["had not posted","hadn't posted"],["'d have found","would have found","would've found"]],"h":["had not posted","would have found"]},{"i":"k1-12","s":"k1","t":"gap","x":"I ___ (pass) the test if I ___ (read) the right chapter.","f":"\"Would have\" goes in the main part. The if-clause takes had + third form.","g":"T3","a":[["'d have passed","would have passed","would've passed"],["'d read","had read"]],"h":["would have passed","had read"]},{"i":"k1-13","s":"k1","t":"gap","x":"If we ___ (leave) ten minutes earlier, we ___ (not / miss) the train.","f":"Type 3: if + had + third form, would not have + third form.","g":"T3","a":[["'d left","had left"],["would not have missed","wouldn't have missed"]],"h":["had left","would not have missed"]},{"i":"k1-14","s":"k1","t":"gap","x":"What ___ (you / say) if she ___ (ask) you to dance?","f":"The question is would + subject + have + third form. The if-clause takes had + third form.","g":"T3","a":[["would you have said"],["'d asked","had asked"]],"h":["would you have said","had asked"]},{"i":"k1-15","s":"k1","t":"gap","x":"If my brother ___ (not / eat) my leftovers, I ___ (not / lock) the fridge.","f":"Type 3 with two negatives: had not + third form, would not have + third form.","g":"T3","a":[["had not eaten","hadn't eaten"],["would not have locked","wouldn't have locked"]],"h":["had not eaten","would not have locked"]},{"i":"k1-16","s":"k1","t":"gap","x":"If Apollo 11 ___ (not / land) safely in July 1969, Neil Armstrong ___ (not / walk) on the moon that day.","f":"Type 3: had not + third form, would not have + third form.","g":"T3","a":[["had not landed","hadn't landed"],["would not have walked","wouldn't have walked"]],"h":["had not landed","would not have walked"]},{"i":"k1-17","s":"k1","t":"fix","x":"If you *would have told* me, I would have saved you a seat.","f":"There is no \"would have\" in the if-clause: If you had told me …","g":"T3","a":[["'d told","had told"]],"h":["had told"]},{"i":"k1-18","s":"k1","t":"fix","x":"If I *had seen* the step, I would not have dropped the cake.","f":"The if-clause takes had + third form, so \"had seen\" is correct.","g":"T3","a":[["OK"]],"h":["OK"]},{"i":"k2-01","s":"k2","t":"mc","x":"I ___ you as soon as the film ___. Don't wait up.","f":"After \"as soon as\" you use the simple present, not \"will\".","g":"WH","c":"will text … ends","w":["text … will end","will text … will end"]},{"i":"k2-02","s":"k2","t":"mc","x":"You won't get better ___ you practise. Sorry, there is no trick.","f":"\"Unless\" means \"if … not\": you won't get better if you don't practise.","g":"UN","c":"unless","w":["if","when"]},{"i":"k2-03","s":"k2","t":"mc","x":"___ I'm 18, I'm going to get my driving licence.","f":"Turning 18 is sure to happen, so it is \"when\", not \"if\".","g":"WH","c":"When","w":["If","Unless"]},{"i":"k2-04","s":"k2","t":"mc","x":"We ___ here until the rain ___.","f":"After \"until\" you use the simple present, not \"will\".","g":"WH","c":"will stay … stops","w":["stay … will stop","will stay … will stop"]},{"i":"k2-05","s":"k2","t":"mc","x":"Which sentence means the same as \"We'll be late if we don't run\"?","f":"\"Unless\" already means \"if … not\", so there is no second \"not\".","g":"UN","c":"We'll be late unless we run.","w":["We'll be late unless we don't run."]},{"i":"k2-06","s":"k2","t":"mc","x":"___ it rains tomorrow, we'll play inside. But the forecast looks fine.","f":"Rain is only possible here, not sure, so it is \"if\".","g":"WH","c":"If","w":["When","Unless"]},{"i":"k2-07","s":"k2","t":"mc","x":"Mum says I can't go out unless I ___ my room first.","f":"After \"unless\" you use the simple present, and there is no extra \"not\".","g":"UN","c":"tidy","w":["will tidy","don't tidy"]},{"i":"k2-08","s":"k2","t":"mc","x":"Call me when you ___ at the station, and I ___ you up.","f":"After \"when\" you use the simple present. \"Will\" goes in the other part.","g":"WH","c":"arrive … will pick","w":["will arrive … pick","will arrive … will pick"]},{"i":"k2-09","s":"k2","t":"mc","x":"You are leaving for a trip. Which sentence is correct?","f":"After \"as soon as\" you use the simple present, not \"will\".","g":"WH","c":"I'll send you a photo as soon as we get there.","w":["I'll send you a photo as soon as we will get there.","I send you a photo as soon as we will get there."]},{"i":"k2-10","s":"k2","t":"gap","x":"I ___ (tell) you everything when I ___ (see) you tomorrow.","f":"\"Will\" goes in the main part. After \"when\" you use the simple present.","g":"WH","a":[["'ll tell","will tell"],["see"]],"h":["will tell","see"]},{"i":"k2-11","s":"k2","t":"gap","x":"She won't talk to you unless you ___ (say) sorry first.","f":"After \"unless\" you use the simple present.","g":"UN","a":[["say"]],"h":["say"]},{"i":"k2-12","s":"k2","t":"gap","x":"As soon as my sister ___ (move) out, I ___ (take) her room.","f":"After \"as soon as\" you use the simple present: moves. \"Will\" goes in the other part.","g":"WH","a":[["moves"],["'ll take","will take"]],"h":["moves","will take"]},{"i":"k2-13","s":"k2","t":"gap","x":"The climate activists say they won't leave the square until the mayor ___ (talk) to them.","f":"After \"until\" you use the simple present, not \"will\".","g":"WH","a":[["talks"]],"h":["talks"]},{"i":"k2-14","s":"k2","t":"gap","x":"We'll lose again unless the coach ___ (change) something.","f":"After \"unless\" you use the simple present: changes.","g":"UN","a":[["changes"]],"h":["changes"]},{"i":"k2-15","s":"k2","t":"gap","x":"When the holidays ___ (start), I ___ (sleep) for three days.","f":"After \"when\" you use the simple present. \"Will\" goes in the other part.","g":"WH","a":[["start"],["'ll sleep","will sleep"]],"h":["start","will sleep"]},{"i":"k2-16","s":"k2","t":"gap","x":"I ___ (not / speak) to him until he ___ (apologise).","f":"\"Will not\" goes in the main part. After \"until\" you use the simple present.","g":"WH","a":[["will not speak","won't speak"],["apologises","apologizes"]],"h":["will not speak","apologises"]},{"i":"k2-17","s":"k2","t":"fix","x":"I'll ring you when I *will be* on the train.","f":"After \"when\" you use the simple present, not \"will\".","g":"WH","a":[["am"]],"h":["am"]},{"i":"k2-18","s":"k2","t":"fix","x":"You can't come in unless you *know* the password.","f":"After \"unless\" you use the simple present, so \"know\" is correct.","g":"UN","a":[["OK"]],"h":["OK"]},{"i":"kc-01","s":"kc","t":"mc","x":"If I ___ about the traffic, I ___ the train this morning.","f":"\"This morning\" is over, so it is too late: type 3.","g":"T3","c":"had known … would have taken","w":["knew … would take","would have known … had taken"]},{"i":"kc-02","s":"kc","t":"mc","x":"You won't get in ___ you are on the guest list. They check every name.","f":"\"Unless\" means \"if … not\": you won't get in if you are not on the list.","g":"UN","c":"unless","w":["if","when"]},{"i":"kc-03","s":"kc","t":"mc","x":"Which sentence tells you that Noor did not study?","f":"Type 3 looks back at something that did not happen.","g":"T3","c":"If Noor had studied, she would have passed.","w":["If Noor studies, she will pass."]},{"i":"kc-04","s":"kc","t":"mc","x":"I ___ you the photos as soon as I ___ home.","f":"After \"as soon as\" you use the simple present, not \"will\".","g":"WH","c":"will send … get","w":["send … will get","will send … will get"]},{"i":"kc-05","s":"kc","t":"mc","x":"If I ___ in a band now, I ___ the drums. I have no talent, but I'm loud.","f":"This is only imagined, and it is about now: type 2.","g":"T2","c":"were … would play","w":["had been … would have played","am … would play"]},{"i":"kc-06","s":"kc","t":"gap","x":"If you ___ (tell) me yesterday, I would have brought my charger.","f":"\"Would have brought\" shows type 3, so the if-clause takes had + third form.","g":"T3","a":[["'d told","had told"]],"h":["had told"]},{"i":"kc-07","s":"kc","t":"gap","x":"If she doesn't answer, I ___ (try) her sister.","f":"\"Doesn't answer\" is simple present, so this is type 1.","g":"T1","a":[["'ll try","will try"]],"h":["will try"]},{"i":"kc-08","s":"kc","t":"gap","x":"If I had my own room, I ___ (paint) the walls black. My sister says no.","f":"\"Had\" is simple past, so this is type 2: would + base form.","g":"T2","a":[["'d paint","would paint"]],"h":["would paint"]},{"i":"kc-09","s":"kc","t":"gap","x":"I won't believe it until I ___ (see) it with my own eyes.","f":"After \"until\" you use the simple present, not \"will\".","g":"WH","a":[["see"]],"h":["see"]},{"i":"kc-10","s":"kc","t":"gap","x":"We ___ (not / miss) the last tram last night if you had looked at the timetable.","f":"\"Had looked\" shows type 3: would not have + third form.","g":"T3","a":[["would not have missed","wouldn't have missed"]],"h":["would not have missed"]},{"i":"kc-11","s":"kc","t":"fix","x":"We would have had more fun if it *would not have rained* all weekend.","f":"There is no \"would have\" in the if-clause: if it had not rained.","g":"T3","a":[["had not rained","hadn't rained"]],"h":["had not rained"]},{"i":"kc-12","s":"kc","t":"gap","x":"Unless it ___ (snow) tonight, we ___ (have) training tomorrow as usual.","f":"After \"unless\" you use the simple present. \"Will\" goes in the other part.","g":"UN","a":[["snows"],["'ll have","will have"]],"h":["snows","will have"]},{"i":"p1-01","s":"p1","t":"mc","x":"I wish I ___ a bit taller. I can't reach anything in this kitchen.","f":"\"I wish\" about now takes the simple past: I wish I were taller.","g":"WI","c":"were","w":["would be","am"]},{"i":"p1-02","s":"p1","t":"mc","x":"I wish I ___ that message last night. Now everybody has seen it.","f":"\"I wish\" about the past takes had + third form.","g":"WI","c":"hadn't sent","w":["didn't send","wouldn't send"]},{"i":"p1-03","s":"p1","t":"mc","x":"You ___ us you were vegetarian. We made chicken for twelve people.","f":"It was a mistake not to do it: should have + third form.","g":"SH","c":"should have told","w":["should tell","should told"]},{"i":"p1-04","s":"p1","t":"mc","x":"Which sentence tells you that Jonas did not come?","f":"\"Had come\" looks back at one moment in the past: he did not come.","g":"WI","c":"\"I wish Jonas had come.\"","w":["\"I wish Jonas came more often.\""]},{"i":"p1-05","s":"p1","t":"mc","x":"I ___ that third energy drink. My hands are shaking.","f":"It was a mistake to do it: should not have + third form.","g":"SH","c":"shouldn't have had","w":["shouldn't had","didn't should have"]},{"i":"p1-06","s":"p1","t":"mc","x":"I wish it ___ Friday already. This week has had about nine days.","f":"\"I wish\" about now takes the simple past: I wish it were Friday.","g":"WI","c":"were","w":["would be","is"]},{"i":"p1-07","s":"p1","t":"mc","x":"We ___ earlier. Now we are standing at the back and I can only see hair.","f":"It was a mistake not to do it: should have + third form.","g":"SH","c":"should have come","w":["should come","should came"]},{"i":"p1-08","s":"p1","t":"mc","x":"If only I ___ my umbrella. Look at me.","f":"\"If only\" works like \"I wish\". About the past it takes had + third form.","g":"WI","c":"had brought","w":["would bring","bring"]},{"i":"p1-09","s":"p1","t":"mc","x":"Your friend is sorry about last night's argument. Which sentence is correct?","f":"\"I wish\" about the past takes had + third form: hadn't shouted.","g":"WI","c":"\"I wish I hadn't shouted at her.\"","w":["\"I wish I wouldn't have shouted at her.\"","\"I wish I didn't shouted at her.\""]},{"i":"p1-10","s":"p1","t":"gap","x":"I wish I ___ (can) play the guitar. I only know the first three notes of one song.","f":"\"I wish\" about now takes the simple past, and the past of \"can\" is \"could\".","g":"WI","a":[["could"]],"h":["could"]},{"i":"p1-11","s":"p1","t":"gap","x":"I wish I ___ (not / tell) my brother about the surprise. He told everyone within an hour.","f":"\"I wish\" about the past takes had + third form.","g":"WI","a":[["had not told","hadn't told"]],"h":["had not told"]},{"i":"p1-12","s":"p1","t":"gap","x":"You ___ (should / see) his face when he opened the box. Priceless.","f":"You missed it, and that is a pity: should have + third form.","g":"SH","a":[["should have seen","should've seen"]],"h":["should have seen"]},{"i":"p1-13","s":"p1","t":"gap","x":"I wish we ___ (live) closer to each other. Two hours on the bus is a lot for one pizza.","f":"\"I wish\" about now takes the simple past: lived.","g":"WI","a":[["lived"]],"h":["lived"]},{"i":"p1-14","s":"p1","t":"gap","x":"I ___ (should / not / press) that button. The whole screen has gone blue.","f":"It was a mistake to do it: should not have + third form.","g":"SH","a":[["should not have pressed","shouldn't have pressed"]],"h":["should not have pressed"]},{"i":"p1-15","s":"p1","t":"gap","x":"I wish I ___ (revise) for the vocabulary test last night instead of watching cat videos.","f":"\"Last night\" is the past, so \"I wish\" takes had + third form.","g":"WI","a":[["'d revised","had revised"]],"h":["had revised"]},{"i":"p1-16","s":"p1","t":"gap","x":"We ___ (should / book) tickets weeks ago. Now the whole tour is sold out.","f":"It was a mistake not to do it: should have + third form.","g":"SH","a":[["should have booked","should've booked"]],"h":["should have booked"]},{"i":"p1-17","s":"p1","t":"fix","x":"I wish I *would have* a normal family. Mine sings in restaurants.","f":"\"I wish\" about now takes the simple past: I wish I had …","g":"WI","a":[["had"]],"h":["had"]},{"i":"p1-18","s":"p1","t":"fix","x":"You *should have asked* me first. I would have said no, but still.","f":"It was a mistake not to ask, so should have + third form is correct.","g":"SH","a":[["OK"]],"h":["OK"]},{"i":"p2-01","s":"p2","t":"mc","x":"If I ___ my homework last night, I ___ free now.","f":"The if-clause is about last night: had + third form. The result is now: would + base form.","g":"MX","c":"had done … would be","w":["did … would be","had done … would have been"]},{"i":"p2-02","s":"p2","t":"mc","x":"If I ___ you so well, I ___ your story yesterday.","f":"Knowing you is still true now: simple past. Yesterday is the past: would have + third form.","g":"MX","c":"didn't know … would have believed","w":["hadn't known … would believe","don't know … would have believed"]},{"i":"p2-03","s":"p2","t":"mc","x":"Which sentence tells you that the speaker is tired now because of last night?","f":"\"Hadn't watched\" looks back at last night. \"Wouldn't be\" is about now.","g":"MX","c":"If I hadn't watched three more episodes, I wouldn't be so tired.","w":["If I didn't watch so many series, I wouldn't be so tired."]},{"i":"p2-04","s":"p2","t":"mc","x":"We ___ lost right now if you ___ the map at the station.","f":"\"Right now\" is the present: would + base form. Taking the map was in the past: had + third form.","g":"MX","c":"wouldn't be … had taken","w":["wouldn't have been … took","wouldn't be … would have taken"]},{"i":"p2-05","s":"p2","t":"mc","x":"If she ___ afraid of heights, she ___ on the roller coaster with us yesterday.","f":"Her fear is always there: simple past. Yesterday is the past: would have + third form.","g":"MX","c":"weren't … would have come","w":["hadn't been … would come","isn't … would have come"]},{"i":"p2-06","s":"p2","t":"mc","x":"If I ___ breakfast this morning, I ___ so hungry now.","f":"Breakfast was this morning: had + third form. The hunger is now: would + base form.","g":"MX","c":"had eaten … wouldn't be","w":["ate … wouldn't be","had eaten … wouldn't have been"]},{"i":"p2-07","s":"p2","t":"mc","x":"Which sentence is about a mistake in the past and a result now?","f":"\"Wouldn't have to\" is about now. \"Wouldn't have had to\" would be about the past.","g":"MX","c":"If you had saved your file, you wouldn't have to start again.","w":["If you had saved your file, you wouldn't have had to start again."]},{"i":"p2-08","s":"p2","t":"mc","x":"If my parents ___ so strict, I ___ to the festival last summer.","f":"They are strict in general: simple past. Last summer is the past: would have + third form.","g":"MX","c":"weren't … would have gone","w":["hadn't been … would go","aren't … would have gone"]},{"i":"p2-09","s":"p2","t":"mc","x":"I ___ a better mark now if I ___ the second page of the test.","f":"The mark is now: would + base form. Missing the page was in the past: had + third form.","g":"MX","c":"would have … had seen","w":["would have had … saw","would have … would have seen"]},{"i":"p2-10","s":"p2","t":"gap","x":"If I ___ (not / lose) my key yesterday, I ___ (not / be) locked out now.","f":"Losing the key was yesterday: had not + third form. Being locked out is now: would not + base form.","g":"MX","a":[["had not lost","hadn't lost"],["would not be","wouldn't be"]],"h":["had not lost","would not be"]},{"i":"p2-11","s":"p2","t":"gap","x":"If I ___ (be) better at maths, I ___ (finish) yesterday's homework in ten minutes.","f":"Being good at maths is a general thing: simple past. Yesterday's homework is the past: would have + third form.","g":"MX","a":[["'d been","had been","was","were"],["'d have finished","would have finished","would've finished"]],"h":["were","would have finished"]},{"i":"p2-12","s":"p2","t":"gap","x":"If we ___ (take) the earlier train this morning, we ___ (be) at the lake by now.","f":"Taking the train was this morning: had + third form. Being at the lake is now: would + base form.","g":"MX","a":[["'d taken","had taken"],["'d be","would be"]],"h":["had taken","would be"]},{"i":"p2-13","s":"p2","t":"gap","x":"If you ___ (listen) to me last week, you ___ (not / be) in trouble today.","f":"Last week is the past: had + third form. Today is now: would not + base form.","g":"MX","a":[["'d listened","had listened"],["would not be","wouldn't be"]],"h":["had listened","would not be"]},{"i":"p2-14","s":"p2","t":"gap","x":"If my sister ___ (not / be) so stubborn, she ___ (say) sorry days ago.","f":"She is stubborn in general: simple past. \"Days ago\" is the past: would have + third form.","g":"MX","a":[["had not been","hadn't been","was not","wasn't","were not","weren't"],["'d have said","would have said","would've said"]],"h":["were not","would have said"]},{"i":"p2-15","s":"p2","t":"gap","x":"I ___ (still / have) my old phone now if I ___ (not / drop) it in the lake last summer.","f":"\"Now\" takes would + base form. Last summer is the past: had not + third form.","g":"MX","a":[["'d still have","still would have","would still have"],["had not dropped","hadn't dropped"]],"h":["would still have","had not dropped"]},{"i":"p2-16","s":"p2","t":"gap","x":"If I ___ (speak) Spanish, I ___ (understand) the whole film last night. I got about four words.","f":"Speaking Spanish is a general thing: simple past. Last night is the past: would have + third form.","g":"MX","a":[["'d spoken","had spoken","spoke"],["'d have understood","would have understood","would've understood"]],"h":["spoke","would have understood"]},{"i":"p2-17","s":"p2","t":"fix","x":"If I had slept more last night, I *would have been* more awake now.","f":"\"Now\" is the present, so the result takes would + base form.","g":"MX","a":[["'d be","would be"]],"h":["would be"]},{"i":"p2-18","s":"p2","t":"fix","x":"If you *had charged* your phone last night, it would work now.","f":"Charging was last night, so had + third form is correct. The result is now.","g":"MX","a":[["OK"]],"h":["OK"]},{"i":"pc-01","s":"pc","t":"mc","x":"I wish I ___ what to say. Everybody is looking at me.","f":"\"I wish\" about now takes the simple past: knew.","g":"WI","c":"knew","w":["would know","know"]},{"i":"pc-02","s":"pc","t":"mc","x":"If I ___ the earlier bus this morning, I ___ in detention now.","f":"The bus was this morning: had + third form. Detention is now: would + base form.","g":"MX","c":"had caught … wouldn't be","w":["caught … wouldn't be","had caught … wouldn't have been"]},{"i":"pc-03","s":"pc","t":"mc","x":"You ___ me. I waited outside the cinema for forty minutes.","f":"It was a mistake not to do it: should have + third form.","g":"SH","c":"should have called","w":["should call","should called"]},{"i":"pc-04","s":"pc","t":"mc","x":"Which sentence tells you that the speaker bought the shoes?","f":"\"Shouldn't have bought\" means: I bought them, and it was a mistake.","g":"SH","c":"I shouldn't have bought these shoes.","w":["I should have bought these shoes."]},{"i":"pc-05","s":"pc","t":"mc","x":"If I ___ so shy, I ___ to her at the party last week.","f":"Being shy is a general thing: simple past. Last week is the past: would have + third form.","g":"MX","c":"weren't … would have talked","w":["hadn't been … would talk","am not … would have talked"]},{"i":"pc-06","s":"pc","t":"fix","x":"I wish I *didn't say* that yesterday. She hasn't spoken to me since.","f":"\"Yesterday\" is the past, so \"I wish\" takes had + third form.","g":"WI","a":[["had not said","hadn't said"]],"h":["had not said"]},{"i":"pc-07","s":"pc","t":"gap","x":"I wish I ___ (have) a brother who knocks before he comes in.","f":"\"I wish\" about now takes the simple past: had.","g":"WI","a":[["had"]],"h":["had"]},{"i":"pc-08","s":"pc","t":"gap","x":"We ___ (should / leave) earlier. Now the last bus has gone.","f":"It was a mistake not to do it: should have + third form.","g":"SH","a":[["should have left","should've left"]],"h":["should have left"]},{"i":"pc-09","s":"pc","t":"gap","x":"If I ___ (not / spend) all my money on Saturday, I ___ (not / be) broke now.","f":"Saturday is the past: had not + third form. Being broke is now: would not + base form.","g":"MX","a":[["had not spent","hadn't spent"],["would not be","wouldn't be"]],"h":["had not spent","would not be"]},{"i":"pc-10","s":"pc","t":"gap","x":"I wish you ___ (tell) me about the test earlier. I found out five minutes ago.","f":"\"Earlier\" is the past, so \"I wish\" takes had + third form.","g":"WI","a":[["'d told","had told"]],"h":["had told"]},{"i":"pc-11","s":"pc","t":"gap","x":"If my phone ___ (have) a better camera, I ___ (take) a photo of that fox last night.","f":"The camera is a general thing: simple past. Last night is the past: would have + third form.","g":"MX","a":[["'d had","had","had had"],["'d have taken","would have taken","would've taken"]],"h":["had","would have taken"]},{"i":"pc-12","s":"pc","t":"gap","x":"I ___ (should / not / laugh). If I ___ (keep) quiet, he would still be talking to me.","f":"It was a mistake to do it: should not have + third form. Keeping quiet was in the past: had + third form.","g":"SH","a":[["should not have laughed","shouldn't have laughed"],["'d kept","had kept"]],"h":["should not have laughed","had kept"]}]});
